# FERRANTECH — The Digital Experience

Portfolio site for Ayoola Enoch Oluwaferanmi (Ferran).
Static HTML, CSS and JavaScript. No build step, no dependencies to install.

## Run locally

Any static server works:

    npx serve .
    # or
    python3 -m http.server 8080

Then open http://localhost:8080

## Deploy

- **GitHub Pages:** push to `main`, then Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch → `main` / root.
- **Netlify / Vercel / Cloudflare Pages:** point at the repo; no build command, publish directory `/`.

## Before going live

1. **Social share image.** Export `assets/og-image.svg` (or design your own 1200×630) to
   `assets/og-image.png`. Update the `og:url` / `twitter:image` meta tags in `index.html`
   with your real deployed URL — most platforms require absolute URLs.
2. **Canonical URL.** Uncomment and set `<link rel="canonical">` in `index.html`.
3. **Check the links.** The departmental site, GitHub, LinkedIn, X and email are the only
   external destinations. Verify each one resolves.

## Editing content

### Projects — `assets/js/data.js` → `PROJECTS`

- Reorder the array to change display order; the item with `featured: true` gets the
  large layout.
- Add `live` or `source` only when a real URL exists. Missing links render as a dashed
  "not public yet" placeholder — never a dead button.
- `tech` and `features` render only when the arrays contain items. Add confirmed
  technologies only, e.g. `tech: ['HTML', 'CSS', 'JavaScript']`.
- `tone` controls the artwork accent: `accent` (lime), `emerald`, `blue`, `gold`.
- `status` + `tone` pair: `Live`/`live`, `In progress`/`progress`, `Concept`/`concept`.

### Gallery — `assets/js/data.js` → `GALLERY`

Every item currently shows a designed placeholder tile with a "Placeholder" badge.
To use a real image:

1. Save an optimised image (WebP or compressed JPG, ~1600px wide max) to `assets/img/`.
2. Add to the item:
